# (after 0527) nvn/frame-step: pauses, window changes and stalls of 8 vsyncs or more do not raise the hold, and a named pause is not paid back
#
# Upstream:  https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/6ef18a1fd70638e11f74ad5ae6144673870a5b45  ("nvn/fstep: ignore pauses and window switches for hold steps and payback (PR #3174)")
#            author seedds, 2026-11-23 01:50 +0800; Co-authored-by: Flying Saucer Studios
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds (nxnative LICENSE); ported from seedds/nxnative, MIT. The attribution above is kept as the licence asks.
#
# Why: a pause (Home, focus lost), a resume or a window change came back as one long frame plus a few late ones: the frame step counted them as the scene's cost, stepped the hold up
#   (60 -> 30 fps after a pause) and paid the pause back as debt (upstream PR #3174).
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_fstep.h, hle_nvn.c, dm/host/dm.h; tests t_fstep, t_nvn): a frame shown 8 vsyncs or more (FSTEP_STALL, 133 ms) or one the host names (settle: focus
#   regained, dm_fstep_settle) is a stall: not late, its time kept out of the hold timers and averages, and the 30 frames after it (FSTEP_GRACE) do not count toward a step up, fine mode
#   or a trial's end; a named pause's time beyond the hold is dropped, not debt. Focus and settle counters are snapshotted at the frame's acquire so a pause lands on the frame it spans.
# Adapted: two hunks by hand (gfx_resume_locked is dm_gfx_suspend(0) here: it calls dm_fstep_settle; g_fs.settle beside 0503's g_fs.nopay). Reconciled with 0503 (DM_FPS_PAYBACK=off):
#   nopay still lets every debt go, so a stall is never paid back with payback off either (a check added to t_fstep). The Mac / iOS front-end hooks (front_mac.m, dm/ios) are not taken:
#   this app's front end is its own; the app's suspend / resume reach dm_gfx_suspend, and focus regained reaches dm_focus_in_since.
# Games: every game with a frame cap (Ocarina of Time at 30 fps). Switches: none new (DM_FPS_PAYBACK is 0503's).
# Tests (M1 Pro): t_fstep 147 checks (upstream's stall cases and ours), t_nvn 513 (fstep_tick settle alignment); in HOST_TESTS. NOT run on a device.
# Shader chain: not touched (b24b25240cad; scripts/build-host.sh checks it).
# Apply with: patch -p1, to the tree out-stage/out-engine/engine + engine-patches/0401..0527, in the order of the numbers of this folder (scripts/build-host.sh does).

